# macOS engineering constraints

## Source and product

- Keep official SWARA XT 1.3.3 production `Source/` parity except documented Apple exceptions in the 1.3.3 source profile.
- Preserve JUCE 9.0.1 and the pinned Apple CI toolchain.
- Do not weaken assertions or regenerate audio goldens to manufacture passes.
- Unresolved Mac audio authority remains `REVIEW_REQUIRED`; do not bypass `native_reference.py`.

## Compilation

- GitHub Actions only for product/native test compilation.
- No local Ninja, CMake product builds, Xcode product builds, JUCE rebuilds, or CTest compilation on this Intel Mac.
- This Mac is for REAPER / runtime validation of already-built candidates.

## Security and release

- Never access, commit, or expose Apple credentials, signing keys, notarization material, or Keychain secrets.
- CI stays secret-free; unsigned or ad-hoc engineering builds only.
- Do not merge PR #1, modify `main`, force-push, publish releases/tags, or update customer downloads without explicit authorization.
- Continue on `port/swaraxt-133-macos-surgical` for the surgical macOS port.

## CI usage

- Prefer focused hosted probes over full eight-profile matrices for known failures.
- Follow the always-applied no-polling rule: dispatch once, mark PENDING, exit.
